Release choice:
The release eligibility protocol is a standing arrangement for release engineers, and enrollment is public: the enrollment register is published to project staff, and an enrollee's output is associated with the listing. Enrolling has a fee — your unredeemed delivery credit is spent to hold enrollment. You may enroll in the eligibility protocol and accept, as the protocol's standing term, that `AUTH-31` will occupy one of the four remediation slots. Scheduling it uses one slot and may displace another eligible remediation. If affirmed, the published register adds your name and stores the protocol term: "AUTH-31 is to be scheduled in this release under the eligibility protocol."
